---
description: Time-series data safety (leakage, CV, target construction)
globs: services/ml/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

# Leakage
- Feature at time t may only use data with timestamp < t. Add `assert` in tests.
- Never reuse a scaler/encoder fit on the full dataset.

# Cross-validation
- Use time-aware validation such as walk-forward splits for forecasting and strategy work.
- No `shuffle=True` on time series.

# Targets
- Define horizon explicitly: `y = close.shift(-h) / close - 1`.
- Align features and target with `pd.concat([X, y], axis=1).dropna()` and commit a length assert.

# Evaluation
- Report out-of-sample metrics, not just in-sample results.
- Compare strategies against a simple baseline such as buy-and-hold when it makes sense.
